diff --git a/CHANGES.md b/CHANGES.md
index fec341e..5b1d59e 100644
--- a/CHANGES.md
+++ b/CHANGES.md
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 * When a `sizes` attribute is allowed on an `img` or `<source>` element (e.g. alongside `srcset` in a responsive-image safelist), the `Cleaner` now validates and rewrites it entry by entry, matching the `srcset` handling. The value is split only on top-level commas, so commas, whitespace, and operators nested inside parentheses stay with their entry; a media condition is optional but, when present, must be a non-empty, parenthesis-balanced expression over a restricted character set (alphanumerics, whitespace, hyphens, colons, dots, the `< = >` comparison operators, and nested parentheses); it need not be wrapped in an outer parenthesized group, so a bare media type such as `screen` is accepted, with no semicolons, braces, quotes, control characters, `url()`/`data:`/script-scheme fragments, and it must be followed by a length. A length is either zero or a non-negative decimal number with one of the `px, em, rem, vw, vh, vmin, vmax, ch, ex, %` units, or a balanced `calc()` expression containing only those units, non-negative numbers, whitespace, and the `+ - * /` operators (no leading minus, empty operand, URL, semicolon, or unbalanced parenthesis). A single corrupted entry is dropped without swallowing later legal entries (parsing resynchronizes at the next comma after an unbalanced group), surviving entries that normalize to an identical spelling are emitted only once at their first position, delimiting quotes and surrounding whitespace are removed, and surviving entries are rejoined with a stable `", "`; if no entry survives, the attribute is removed rather than left empty. The same `sizes` input on a `source` and an `img` is always rewritten to a byte-identical value, and each element is handled independently: a bad `sizes` value never affects that element's `srcset`, `src`, `media`, `type`, children, or sibling order, and a valid `sizes` never relaxes `srcset` protocol checks or lets a `source` policy widen the `img`. As with `srcset`, `sizes` is special-cased only on `img`/`source`: when it is not in the attribute whitelist it is removed exactly like any other disallowed attribute, and on other elements it keeps ordinary attribute treatment. Cleaning returns a new document without mutating the input, and the result is stable across a second clean and a serialize-reparse-clean round trip.

 ### Bug Fixes
+* Hardened the entry-by-entry `sizes` cleaner against pathological attribute values so they cannot be used for CPU or stack exhaustion: duplicate detection is now constant-time (a value with many distinct entries was previously quadratic), entry splitting after unbalanced parentheses is a single linear pass rather than rescanning the remainder for each malformed group, and `calc()` validation is iterative with no per-nesting substring copy, so a deeply nested `calc()` no longer overflows the stack or allocates quadratic memory. The accepted/rejected output for every input is unchanged.
 * Fixed handling of null characters and initial newlines in HTML to better match the HTML spec, including `pre`, `listing`, and `textarea` elements. Leading newlines in these elements' text are preserved when saving and reparsing HTML. [#2616](https://github.com/jhy/jsoup/pull/2616)

